There is a *GREAT* multiplayer, nethack-like game called "Crossfire".
It is written for X-Windows so you cannot play it on terminals.  Anyway
the game is outstanding.   

The game is a bit of a mixture of NetHack, Ultima and Gauntlet.   Muliple
Players can join the game simultaneously.   You choose a character class
(like Fighter, Mage, Cleric, Babarian, etc) and then you go out for monster
hunt.   There are many, many (~300) dungeons where you can slaughter monsters,
collect weapons, armour, potions, scrolls and other items.   You can cast
spells, transact with other players and do many things more.  Everything is
displayed in nice graphics, different monsters may have different sizes 
and all monsters move around.

The game is still under developement, so expect some bugs but all in all it
is already quite stable.   You will need the game itself (about 500k) and
the maps (about 1.200k).   Crossfire comes with a level editor which you
can use to design your own dungeons.

The game should be available on many archive sites, use some archie tool
to find out which is next to your site (search for substring 'crossfire').
If you have no archie access feel free to ask me.

